.\" The manual page of one command of example-cli, the imaginary inventory
.\" program of the command pack's test stand. Written for the tests: it
.\" describes nothing real. One entry disagrees with the program's help, and
.\" one is in a form the reader does not take, on purpose.
.TH EXAMPLE-CLI-ITEM-LIST 1 2026-11-18 "example-cli 2.4.1" "example-cli manual"
.SH NAME
example-cli-item-list \- list the items
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B example-cli item list
[\fB\-\-location\fR \fIcode\fR] [\fB\-\-ref\fR \fIreference\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fIform\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the items of the inventory, one a line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-location\fR \fIcode\fR
Only the items at this location, such as A01.
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR
Only the item with this reference.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIform\fR
How to print them: table, json, or jsonl.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR
At most N items, a whole number.
.TP
\fB\-\-colour\fR[=\fIwhen\fR]
Whether to colour the table.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the items were listed.
